{"actions":[],"cardId":"cardid_3499b675ea28cbd97d56d82fa30f46b2","createdAt":"2026-03-15T00:18:56Z","expiresAt":"2026-03-17T00:18:56Z","icon":"square.grid.2x2","id":"card_8b5de54b39bc3272abe743fce4eae1eb","message":"An IRGC ballistic missile struck Prince Sultan Air Base, damaging five KC-135 Stratotankers — the backbone of US aerial refueling operations in the region.","metadata":{"height":440,"htmlContent":"<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset='utf-8'><meta name='viewport' content='width=device-width,initial-scale=1'><meta name='color-scheme' content='light dark'><style>:root{--bg:var(--fw-bg,#ffffff);--text:var(--fw-text,#111827);--muted:var(--fw-text-secondary,#6b7280);--tertiary:var(--fw-text-tertiary,#9ca3af);--border:var(--fw-border,rgba(15,23,42,0.08));--accent:var(--fw-accent,#2563eb);--surface:var(--fw-surface,#f3f4f6)}@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){:root{--bg:var(--fw-bg,#1c1c1e);--text:var(--fw-text,#f2f2f7);--muted:var(--fw-text-secondary,#a0a0a0);--tertiary:var(--fw-text-tertiary,#707070);--border:var(--fw-border,rgba(255,255,255,0.1));--accent:var(--fw-accent,#4b93ff);--surface:var(--fw-surface,#2a2a2a)}}body{margin:0;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--text);background:var(--bg)}*{box-sizing:border-box}a.card-link{display:block;text-decoration:none;color:inherit;cursor:pointer}a.card-link:active{opacity:0.7}.hero-img{width:100%;height:clamp(120px,34vw,220px);object-fit:cover;display:block;background:var(--border)}.content{padding:16px 20px 20px}.headline{font-size:18px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.3;margin:0 0 6px;color:var(--text)}.source{font-size:13px;color:var(--tertiary);font-weight:500;margin:0 0 10px}.summary{font-size:15px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.55;margin:0 0 14px}.stats{display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap}.stat{background:var(--surface);padding:8px 12px;border-radius:8px;font-size:12px;line-height:1.3}.stat-val{font-weight:700;font-size:14px;color:var(--text);display:block;margin-bottom:2px}.stat-lbl{color:var(--tertiary)}</style></head><body><a class='card-link' href='https://theaviationist.com/2026/03/14/five-tankers-damaged-at-psab/' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer'><img class='hero-img' src='https://theaviationist.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Five-KC-135s-damaged.jpeg' alt='KC-135 tankers at Prince Sultan Air Base' onerror=\"this.style.display='none'\"><div class='content'><div class='headline'>Five US Tankers Hit in Iranian Strike on Saudi Base</div><div class='source'>The Aviationist · Mar 14, 2026</div><div class='summary'>An IRGC ballistic missile struck Prince Sultan Air Base deep in the Saudi interior, damaging five KC-135 Stratotankers on the ground. No casualties, but the refuelers are the backbone of US air operations. PSAB is 600 km from the Iranian coast — a ballistic missile covers that in 6–8 minutes. Despite the damage, tankers tracked online were still flying missions from the base hours later.</div><div class='stats'><div class='stat'><span class='stat-val'>5 tankers</span><span class='stat-lbl'>Damaged in this strike</span></div><div class='stat'><span class='stat-val'>6–8 min</span><span class='stat-lbl'>Missile flight time</span></div><div class='stat'><span class='stat-val'>600 km</span><span class='stat-lbl'>PSAB from Iran</span></div></div></div></a></body></html>","web_images":[{"image_url":"https://theaviationist.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Five-KC-135s-damaged.jpeg","source_url":"https://theaviationist.com/2026/03/14/five-tankers-damaged-at-psab"}]},"priority":"medium","state":"active","subType":"articles","subtitle":"The Aviationist · Mar 14, 2026","timestamp":"2026-03-15T00:18:56Z","title":"Five US Tankers Hit in Iranian Strike on Saudi Base","type":"html-webview"}
{"actions":[],"cardId":"cardid_3499b675ea28cbd97d56d82fa30f46b2","createdAt":"2026-03-15T00:18:56Z","expiresAt":"2026-03-17T00:18:56Z","icon":"square.grid.2x2","id":"card_9b3aec063a69acef0524774daa1f3ac9","message":"All-white ceramic case, frosted zigzag dial, titanium accents — Omega's boldest Olympic diver yet. €10,500 retail.","metadata":{"height":460,"htmlContent":"<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset='utf-8'><meta name='viewport' content='width=device-width,initial-scale=1'><meta name='color-scheme' content='light dark'><style>:root{--bg:var(--fw-bg,#ffffff);--text:var(--fw-text,#111827);--muted:var(--fw-text-secondary,#6b7280);--tertiary:var(--fw-text-tertiary,#9ca3af);--border:var(--fw-border,rgba(15,23,42,0.08));--accent:var(--fw-accent,#2563eb);--surface:var(--fw-surface,#f3f4f6)}@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){:root{--bg:var(--fw-bg,#1c1c1e);--text:var(--fw-text,#f2f2f7);--muted:var(--fw-text-secondary,#a0a0a0);--tertiary:var(--fw-text-tertiary,#707070);--border:var(--fw-border,rgba(255,255,255,0.1));--accent:var(--fw-accent,#4b93ff);--surface:var(--fw-surface,#2a2a2a)}}body{margin:0;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--text);background:var(--bg)}*{box-sizing:border-box}a.card-link{display:block;text-decoration:none;color:inherit;cursor:pointer}a.card-link:active{opacity:0.7}.hero-img{width:100%;height:clamp(120px,34vw,220px);object-fit:cover;display:block;background:var(--border)}.content{padding:16px 20px 20px}.headline{font-size:18px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.3;margin:0 0 6px;color:var(--text)}.source{font-size:13px;color:var(--tertiary);font-weight:500;margin:0 0 10px}.summary{font-size:15px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.55;margin:0 0 14px}.specs{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px}.spec{background:var(--surface);padding:6px 10px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;color:var(--text);font-weight:500}</style></head><body><a class='card-link' href='https://precisionwatches.com/journal/omega-seamaster-300m-milano-cortina-2026-review/' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer'><img class='hero-img' src='https://precisionwatches.com/wp-content/uploads/Omega_SeamasterDiver300MMilanoCortina2026_1100x667_1.jpg' alt='Omega Seamaster 300M Milano Cortina 2026 white ceramic' onerror=\"this.style.display='none'\"><div class='content'><div class='headline'>Omega's White Ceramic Seamaster for Milano Cortina 2026</div><div class='source'>Precision Watches · Review</div><div class='summary'>Omega's third Milano Cortina Olympic watch is the boldest — an all-white 43.5mm ceramic Seamaster Diver 300M. The frosted dial has a laser-engraved zigzag pattern inspired by the Games' \"26\" emblem, visible as you tilt the watch. Rhodium-plated hands, grade 5 titanium accents, Co-Axial Master Chronometer 8806 movement, and a gradient-blue seconds hand break the monotone. White rubber strap, no date window. Wears smaller than 43.5mm thanks to downward-curving lugs.</div><div class='specs'><span class='spec'>43.5mm ceramic</span><span class='spec'>€10,500</span><span class='spec'>Calibre 8806</span><span class='spec'>300m WR</span><span class='spec'>Grade 5 Ti</span><span class='spec'>No date</span></div></div></a></body></html>","web_images":[{"image_url":"https://precisionwatches.com/wp-content/uploads/Omega_SeamasterDiver300MMilanoCortina2026_1100x667_1.jpg","source_url":"https://precisionwatches.com/journal/omega-seamaster-300m-milano-cortina-2026-review"}]},"priority":"medium","state":"active","subType":"articles","subtitle":"Precision Watches · Jan 2026","timestamp":"2026-03-15T00:18:56Z","title":"Omega's White Ceramic Seamaster for Milano Cortina 2026","type":"html-webview"}
{"actions":[],"cardId":"cardid_7bd4a4917fc8e113c9d6874ce5e404d8","createdAt":"2026-03-15T00:18:56Z","expiresAt":"2026-03-17T00:18:56Z","icon":"square.grid.2x2","id":"card_570568def4cce60e0a92b45f85a8cdc1","message":"A service charging to remove the recording LED from Ray-Ban Meta glasses has 48K likes and a firestorm of comments about consent and covert filming.","metadata":{"height":560,"htmlContent":"<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset='utf-8'><meta name='viewport' content='width=device-width,initial-scale=1'><meta name='color-scheme' content='light dark'><style>:root{--bg:var(--fw-bg,#ffffff);--text:var(--fw-text,#111827);--muted:var(--fw-text-secondary,#6b7280);--tertiary:var(--fw-text-tertiary,#9ca3af);--border:var(--fw-border,rgba(15,23,42,0.08));--accent:var(--fw-accent,#2563eb);--surface:var(--fw-surface,#f3f4f6)}@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){:root{--bg:var(--fw-bg,#1c1c1e);--text:var(--fw-text,#f2f2f7);--muted:var(--fw-text-secondary,#a0a0a0);--tertiary:var(--fw-text-tertiary,#707070);--border:var(--fw-border,rgba(255,255,255,0.1));--accent:var(--fw-accent,#4b93ff);--surface:var(--fw-surface,#2a2a2a)}}body{margin:0;padding:20px;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--text);background:var(--bg)}*{box-sizing:border-box}h4{font-size:18px;margin:0 0 4px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.3}.subtitle{font-size:14px;color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 10px;line-height:1.4}.msg{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 16px;line-height:1.5}.divider{border:none;border-top:1px solid var(--border);margin:0}.point{padding:12px 0;font-size:14px;line-height:1.4}.point strong{font-weight:600}.point-detail{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);margin:2px 0 0}.carousel-inner{display:flex;gap:10px;padding:16px 0 4px;overflow-x:auto;scrollbar-width:none;justify-content:flex-start;justify-content:safe center}.carousel-inner::-webkit-scrollbar{display:none}.carousel-inner a{display:block;position:relative;min-width:156px;width:156px;aspect-ratio:9/16;border-radius:14px;overflow:hidden;text-decoration:none;background:var(--surface);flex-shrink:0}.carousel-inner a .placeholder{width:100%;height:100%;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:28px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--surface) 0%,var(--border) 100%)}.carousel-label{position:absolute;left:0;right:0;bottom:0;padding:10px 10px;background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(0,0,0,0) 0%,rgba(0,0,0,0.72) 100%);color:#fff;font-size:12px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.3}</style></head><body><h4>Meta glasses LED removal goes viral</h4><div class='subtitle'>The privacy debate your wearables team should know about</div><p class='msg'>A service offering to remove the recording LED from Ray-Ban Meta glasses has 48K likes. Comments split between people asking \"how much?\" and people calling it \"creepy.\" Swedish media investigations and YouTube tutorials have amplified the trend.</p><hr class='divider'><div class='point'><strong>The tension</strong><div class='point-detail'>Meta added the LED specifically as a privacy safeguard — a visible signal that recording is active. A cottage industry now exists to disable it, undermining the consent mechanism the hardware was designed to enforce.</div></div><hr class='divider'><div class='point'><strong>Legal gray zone</strong><div class='point-detail'>Two-party consent states make covert recording illegal. The comment thread is full of demands for legal clarification, with some users defending it for evidence-gathering and others flagging it as enabling surveillance.</div></div><hr class='divider'><section data-feed-media-carousel=\"1\" style=\"margin-top:12px;\"><div class=\"carousel-inner\" style=\"display:flex;gap:10px;overflow-x:auto;padding:2px 8px 4px;scroll-snap-type:x mandatory;-webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch;justify-content:flex-start;justify-content:safe center;\"><a href=\"https://instagram.com/reel/DVhEOMrkhW2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"display:block;flex:0 0 156px;width:156px;min-heigh