dth:156px;aspect-ratio:9/16;border-radius:14px;overflow:hidden;text-decoration:none;background:var(--surface);flex-shrink:0}.carousel-inner a .placeholder{width:100%;height:100%;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:28px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#1a1a2e 0%,#16213e 50%,#0f3460 100%)}.carousel-label{position:absolute;left:0;right:0;bottom:0;padding:10px 10px;background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(0,0,0,0) 0%,rgba(0,0,0,0.72) 100%);color:#fff;font-size:12px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.3}</style></head><body><h4>Indie roguelike trailers — 2 reels</h4><div class='subtitle'>Pixel-art dungeon crawlers shipping this week on Instagram</div><hr class='divider'><div class='post'><div class='post-text'>Two indie devs are launching pixel-art roguelikes right now. \"Slay the Dungeon\" is a mobile dungeon crawler with turn-based combat, and @redcorngames is building a deck-builder with a mechanic they claim has never existed. Both are solo/duo teams — similar scale to your MRBD games, different platforms.</div><div class='author'><div class='author-avatar'>V</div><span class='author-handle'>@drtamagotchi</span><span class='author-likes'>· 18 likes · Posted today</span></div></div><hr class='divider'><section data-feed-media-carousel=\"1\" style=\"margin-top:12px;\"><div class=\"carousel-inner\" style=\"display:flex;gap:10px;overflow-x:auto;padding:2px 8px 4px;scroll-snap-type:x mandatory;-webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch;justify-content:flex-start;justify-content:safe center;\"><a href=\"https://instagram.com/reel/DV3yLIIACDl\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"display:block;flex:0 0 156px;width:156px;min-height:222px;aspect-ratio:9/16;border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;text-decoration:none;background:var(--fw-surface-muted,rgba(15,23,42,0.08));scroll-snap-align:start;\"><video src=\"https://scontent-ord5-2.cdninstagram.com/o1/v/t16/f2/m69/AQOczsDo_PvM_9_5n02hv3vp1bbiXeYShpx2snLt7bUoaP2J46vDMB8xZgDajifkY2UCgIe7EHCa0LRI43ZuAb